content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-114, AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-20500, raw-water transfer line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing vibration is 8.3 mm/s. The HF-300 Figure 3 severity zones apply, classifying the highest bearing-housing reading. 8.3 mm/s is above the 7.1 mm/s Zone C/D boundary and within Zone D (7.1 to 11.0 mm/s RMS), labelled 'Damage likely - stop the pump'.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 70 C. The manual limits for housing-surface temperature are: normal up to 70 C, alarm 80 C, trip 90 C. The reading sits exactly at the upper limit of normal. It is below the alarm limit but has no margin.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage was reported. The troubleshooting symptom 'Leakage at shaft seal' is therefore not present, and seal replacement (5.2) is not indicated by the evidence.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing wear is the most likely cause. It is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, and the drive-end housing shows Zone D vibration together with a temperature at the top of the normal range.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is listed as a cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage is listed as a cause of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation (insufficient NPSH) is listed as a cause of high vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is listed as a cause of high bearing temperature. It is less likely to explain the vibration.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump now, because the vibration is in Zone D ('Damage likely - stop the pump'). Do not restart until the cause has been corrected.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening it.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before disturbing anything, check shaft alignment with a laser alignment tool against these tolerances: parallel offset 0.05 mm, angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check the grease quantity in the bearing housings to rule out over-greasing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the bearings. If either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature, replace both as a pair: drive-end 6312-C3 (HF3-512) and non-drive-end 6310-C3 (HF3-510). Follow section 5.3.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg, use lifting equipment). Inspect the impeller (HF3-210) for imbalance or damage. Inspect the shaft sleeve for scoring while it is accessible.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fit a new casing gasket (HF3-120) whenever the casing is opened. Tighten all fasteners to the manual's Table 5, which applies to this serial number. The Table 5 torque values are not in the evidence provided; obtain them before reassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check suction conditions and NPSH to rule out cavitation.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Re-align the shaft with the laser tool after any work that moved the motor or bearing housing. Tolerances: 0.05 mm parallel offset, 0.05 mm per 100 mm angular.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, make sure the casing is primed and the Plan 11 seal flush from discharge is available, because the seal must never run dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After restart, measure vibration on both bearing housings and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Confirm the reading is in Zone A/B (at or below 4.5 mm/s RMS) for long-term operation. Confirm housing temperature stays at or below 70 C, the normal limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3 (replace as a pair if worn)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 (replace as a pair with drive-end bearing)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket (replace whenever casing is opened)",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop the pump immediately. Zone D vibration means damage is likely.",
      "citations": [
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening it.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg. Lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry. Confirm the Plan 11 seal flush before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement (pair): 6.0 hours, 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: 1.5 hours, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical seal replacement (4.0 h, 2 technicians) is not planned, because no leakage was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Service bulletin SB-2026-014 (issued 14 March 2026) supersedes seal HF3-450 with cartridge seal HF3-450B at 30 Nm gland torque. However, it applies only to HF-300 serial HF3-22000 and above. P-114 is serial HF3-20500, which is below that range. The original manual therefore applies: seal HF3-450, sleeve HF3-455 and Table 5 torques. Do not fit HF3-450B or use 30 Nm on this pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Table 5 fastener torque values (casing, impeller nut, gland nut, bearing housing) are not included in the evidence. They must be obtained from the full manual before reassembly.",
    "Was the 8.3 mm/s reading measured as RMS velocity, as Figure 3 requires? The report does not say.",
    "The non-drive-end bearing housing vibration and temperature readings were not reported.",
    "No previous vibration or temperature trend data for P-114 is available to show whether this is a sudden or gradual change.",
    "The evidence does not specify grease type, correct grease quantity or regreasing interval.",
    "The evidence does not provide a detailed step-by-step bearing replacement procedure, bearing fit or clearance values, or impeller balance acceptance criteria.",
    "The evidence does not provide the available NPSH or the required NPSH for the raw-water transfer line.",
    "Site-specific lockout/tagout and electrical isolation requirements for the 55 kW, 400 V motor are not covered by the evidence."
  ]
}
